module_doc:
Clean train/dev in a new corpus, preserving original identities and partitions.

No sealed-test records are opened. Test stays reserved in the original corpus;
it must be re-encoded with this tokenizer only when final evaluation is authorized.

After-training pipeline (never more than 3 GPU processes together with the trainer launcher):
1. evaluate each finished run in a free slot;
2. when the launcher's 12 jobs are done, train K1SC_s1 (diagnostic: K1 with separate clip groups) and
   C0_s3 (third C0 seed), then evaluate them;
3. idle 5 min, solo throughput smokes for all six arms (thermal state recorded before/after);
4. idle 5 min, the 10M benchmark (solo);
5. grad_share, training_summary, compare.

nohup python3 -B -m v11_tiny.post > v11_tiny/runs/post.log 2>&1 &

Ablation (DESIGN_STEPS Step 6.2): XM codes on the VAE's switches.

A trained paper-faithful metacontroller's switch unit is frozen and its posterior-mean pass fixes the segments
(β > 0.5, first step always a switch). K = 8 learned controller codes c_1..c_K (in z-space) replace the Gaussian
posterior. Training is forward explorative modelling in the memory-saving mode (XM App. C):
  1. K no-grad forward passes, pass k assigning code k to every segment; per-segment action NLL ℓ_{s,k}
     (an approximation: other segments' codes in pass k are also k);
  2. per segment, the soft assignment r_{s,k} = softmax_k(−ℓ_{s,k} / τ) (τ → hard best-of-K as τ → 0);
  3. one gradient pass with z_s = Σ_k r_{s,k} c_k... (soft) — here hard: z_s = c_{argmin_k ℓ_{s,k}}, so only the
     best code per segment r

